.TH "Docv::CrystalPages::Renderer" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::CrystalPages::Renderer \- Writes markd blocks as roff.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::CrystalPages::Renderer\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Writes markd blocks as roff. With \fIsections\fR, headings become \fB\%.SH\fR
and \fB\%.SS\fR as on a page of their own; otherwise, inside a page section,
they become bold paragraphs.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBBULLET = "\e\e(bu"\fR
Bullet of unordered list items.
.TP 4
\fBFLAG\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
FLAG = /\eA(BUG|DEPRECATED|EXPERIMENTAL|FIXME|NOTE|OPTIMIZE|TODO|WARNING)(?:\e(([\(ha)]*)\e))?:?(?=\es|\ez)/
.EE
.RE
.PP
Flag words that open a paragraph in Crystal doc comments, shown as
bold labels.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBSECTIONS = {1 => ".SH", 2 => ".SH", 3 => ".SS"}\fR
Roff macro for each heading level when the text is a whole page.
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.PP
\fBdef self.new(io : IO, sections : Bool = false)\fR
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef item(head : String, blocks : Array(Markd::Node)) : Nil\fR
A tagged paragraph: \fIhead\fR is the roff that opens it (\fB\%.IP\fR or \fB\%.TP\fR
and its tag), the first paragraph of \fIblocks\fR continues on it and the
remaining blocks keep its indentation.
.PP
\fBdef render(blocks : Array(Markd::Node)) : Nil\fR
.PP
\fBdef render(block : Markd::Node) : Nil\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef tables? : Bool\fR
Whether a table was written, which needs the \fB\%tbl\fR preprocessor.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/crystal_pages/roff.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "Docv::CrystalPages" (3cr),
.BR "docv" (7cr)
